%% Columns (weight-split regions) and stacks (overlaid, step-swapped layers).
%%   lmr2svg examples/columns/deck.lmr -o columns.html
!title Columns and stacks

!slide Two columns

!columns[3 2]
	!column
		A wider left column (weight 3). Each column flows independently, so its
		prose, lists, and maths wrap to their own sub-region.

		- point one
		- point two
	!column
		A narrower right column (weight 2).

		$a^2 + b^2 = c^2$

!slide Stacked layers

A stack overlays layers in one spot; each `!layer<spec>` says when it shows, and
one takes the place of the previous, so nothing below moves:

!stack
	!layer<0>
		First layer, shown from step 0.
	!layer<1->
		Second layer takes its place from step 1.
